    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<main id="primary" class="site-main container" style="max-width:1200px; margin:0 auto; padding:2rem 1rem;"><article id="post-625" class="cpt-single-product post-625 product type-product status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry product_category-amino-acids" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Product"><section class="product-hero" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2rem;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:2rem;"><div class="product-image" style="flex:1 1 400px;max-width:600px;">
<img src="/images/uploads/2025/09/1-768x768.jpg" width="600" height="600" class="attachment-600x600 size-600x600 wp-post-image" alt="L-Lysine Sulphate 70% (Feed Grade) — Amino Acid Additive for Animal Nutrition" itemprop="image" decoding="async" /></div><div class="product-summary" style="flex:1 1 500px;min-width:280px;"><header class="entry-header"><h1 class="entry-title" itemprop="name" style="font-size:1.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">L-Lysine Sulphate 70% (Feed Grade) — Amino Acid Additive for Animal Nutrition</h1></header><div class="product-feature" style="font-size:1rem;line-height:1.6;opacity:0.9;" itemprop="description"><h2 data-start="1948" data-end="1988">Features</h2><ol data-start="1989" data-end="2609"><li data-start="1989" data-end="2103"><p data-start="1992" data-end="2103"><strong data-start="1992" data-end="2011">Cost efficiency</strong> – lower cost per gram of usable lysine compared to L-Lysine HCl, though dosage is higher.</p></li><li data-start="2255" data-end="2388"><p data-start="2258" data-end="2388"><strong data-start="2258" data-end="2282">High bioavailability</strong> – effectively supplies lysine to swine, poultry, and fish; comparable to L-Lysine HCl in non-ruminants.</p></li><li data-start="2389" data-end="2471"><p data-start="2392" data-end="2471"><strong data-start="2392" data-end="2411">Granulated form</strong> – good flowability, less dust, easy mixing in feed mills.</p></li><li data-start="2472" data-end="2609"><p data-start="2475" data-end="2609"><strong data-start="2475" data-end="2500">Regulatory acceptance</strong> – evaluated as safe and efficacious for non-ruminants by EFSA and widely approved in global feed industry.</p></li></ol><div style="margin-top:1rem;">
