style="display:inline-block;padding:0.6rem 1.2rem;background:#0073aa;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;">
Contact Us
</a></div></div></div></section><section class="product-description entry-content" style="margin-top:2rem;"><h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">Product Description</h2><div itemprop="description"><p data-start="721" data-end="753">Cost-effective <a href="/product/" data-internallinksmanager029f6b8e52c="4" title="Feed additives">feed</a>-grade amino acid source: <strong data-start="515" data-end="540">L-Lysine Sulphate 70%</strong> (≥55% available lysine). Widely applied in poultry, swine, and aquaculture nutrition to optimize growth and feed efficiency. Samples available, bulk packaging customizable.</p><h2 data-start="721" data-end="753">1. Product Names &amp; Synonyms</h2><ul data-start="754" data-end="1038"><li data-start="754" data-end="811"><p data-start="756" data-end="811">Official name: <strong data-start="771" data-end="809">L-Lysine Sulphate 70% (Feed Grade)</strong></p></li><li data-start="812" data-end="920"><p data-start="814" data-end="920">Synonyms: L-lysine sulphate, lysine sulphate (feed grade), 70% lysine sulphate, lysine sulphate granules</p></li><li data-start="921" data-end="948"><p data-start="923" data-end="948">CAS No.: <strong data-start="932" data-end="946">60343-69-3</strong></p></li><li data-start="949" data-end="986"><p data-start="951" data-end="986">Molecular Formula: <strong data-start="970" data-end="984">C₆H₁₆N₂O₆S</strong></p></li><li data-start="987" data-end="1038"><p data-start="989" data-end="1038">Common abbreviation: <strong data-start="1010" data-end="1035">L-Lysine Sulphate 70%</strong></p></li></ul><hr data-start="1040" data-end="1043" /><h2 data-start="1045" data-end="1090">2. Technical Specifications &amp; Properties</h2><p data-start="1092" data-end="1117"><strong data-start="1092" data-end="1115">Guaranteed Analysis</strong></p><ul data-start="1118" data-end="1461"><li data-start="1118" data-end="1155"><p data-start="1120" data-end="1155">L-lysine sulphate (as salt): ~70%</p></li><li data-start="1156" data-end="1196"><p data-start="1158" data-end="1196">Available L-lysine (free base): ≥55%</p></li><li data-start="1197" data-end="1251"><p data-start="1199" data-end="1251">Other amino acids: ≥10% (fermentation by-products)</p></li><li data-start="1252" data-end="1271"><p data-start="1254" data-end="1271">Moisture: ≤3.0%</p></li><li data-start="1272" data-end="1286"><p data-start="1274" data-end="1286">Ash: ≤4.0%</p></li><li data-start="1287" data-end="1331"><p data-start="1289" data-end="1331">pH (1% solution): 3.0–6.5 (typical ≈3.5)</p></li><li data-start="1332" data-end="1358"><p data-start="1334" data-end="1358">Sulphate content: ≤15%</p></li><li data-start="1359" data-end="1384"><p data-start="1361" data-end="1384">Heavy metals: ≤0.003%</p></li><li data-start="1385" data-end="1461"><p data-start="1387" data-end="1461">Shelf life: 24 months (unopened, dry conditions at ambient temperature)</p></li></ul><p data-start="1463" data-end="1488"><strong data-start="1463" data-end="1486">Physical Properties</strong></p><ul data-start="1489" data-end="1718"><li data-start="1489" data-end="1561"><p data-start="1491" data-end="1561">Appearance: light brown to yellowish free-flowing powder or granules</p></li><li data-start="1562" data-end="1619"><p data-start="1564" data-end="1619">Solubility: easily soluble in water, insoluble in oil</p></li><li data-start="1620" data-end="1670"><p data-start="1622" data-end="1670">Bulk density: 600–650 kg/m³ (≈0.60–0.65 g/cm³)</p></li><li data-start="1671" data-end="1718"><p data-start="1673" data-end="1718">Particle size: ≥90% pass 1.55–1.7 mm sieve</p></li></ul><p data-start="1720" data-end="1745"><strong data-start="1720" data-end="1743">Chemical Properties</strong></p><ul data-start="1746" data-end="1941"><li data-start="1746" data-end="1781"><p data-start="1748" data-end="1781">Molecular weight: ~244.26 g/mol</p></li><li data-start="1782" data-end="1851"><p data-start="1784" data-end="1851">Stability: stable under dry, cool, and light-protected conditions</p></li><li data-start="1852" data-end="1941"><p data-start="1854" data-end="1941">Reactivity: Avoid prolonged high-temperature processing to reduce Maillard reactions</p></li></ul><hr data-start="2611" data-end="2614" /><h2 data-start="2616" data-end="2643">4. Application &amp; Usage</h2><p data-start="2645" data-end="2773"><strong data-start="2645" data-end="2668">Calculation Formula</strong><br data-start="2668" data-end="2671" />Required lysine (g/kg) ÷ Available lysine fraction (0.55) = Dosage of L-Lysine Sulphate (g/kg feed).</p><p data-start="2775" data-end="2796"><strong data-start="2775" data-end="2794">Dosage Examples</strong></p><ul data-start="2797" data-end="3007"><li data-start="2797" data-end="2878"><p data-start="2799" data-end="2878">To supply 1.0 g/kg lysine → add <strong data-start="2831" data-end="2858">1.82 g/kg (1.82 kg/ton)</strong> L-Lysine Sulphate</p></li><li data-start="2879" data-end="2942"><p data-start="2881" data-end="2942">To supply 1.5 g/kg lysine → add <strong data-start="2913" data-end="2940">2.73 g/kg (2.73 kg/ton)</strong></p></li><li data-start="2943" data-end="3007"><p data-start="2945" data-end="3007">To supply 2.0 g/kg lysine → add <strong data-start="2977" data-end="3004">3.64 g/kg (3.64 kg/ton)</strong></p></li></ul><p data-start="3009" data-end="3035"><strong data-start="3009" data-end="3033">Species Applications</strong></p><ul data-start="3036" data-end="3537"><li data-start="3036" data-end="3187"><p data-start="3038" data-end="3187"><strong data-start="3038" data-end="3071">Swine (30–60 kg grower pigs):</strong> Target SID lysine ≈0.94% (9.4 g/kg). If basal feed provides 7.5 g/kg, supplement 1.9 g/kg → add <strong data-start="3168" data-end="3183">3.45 kg/ton</strong>.</p></li><li data-start="3188" data-end="3298"><p data-start="3190" data-end="3298"><strong data-start="3190" data-end="3203">Broilers:</strong> Target ≈1.0% lysine. If basal feed has 8.5 g/kg, supplement 1.6 g/kg → add <strong data-start="3279" data-end="3294">2.91 kg/ton</strong>.</p></li><li data-start="3299" data-end="3428"><p data-start="3301" data-end="3428"><strong data-start="3301" data-end="3326">Layers / Aquaculture:</strong> Dosage depends on growth stage; calculate with a formula based on NRC or company nutrition standards.</p></li><li data-start="3429" data-end="3537"><p data-start="3431" data-end="3537"><strong data-start="3431" data-end="3445">Ruminants:</strong> Not effective unless rumen-protected, since unprotected lysine is degraded in the rumen.</p></li></ul><p data-start="3539" data-end="3559"><strong data-start="3539" data-end="3557">Best Practices</strong></p><ul data-start="3560" data-end="3748"><li data-start="3560" data-end="3621"><p data-start="3562" data-end="3621">Pre-mix in small batches before blending into the final feed.</p></li><li data-start="3622" data-end="3682"><p data-start="3624" data-end="3682">Monitor heat treatment (pelleting) to avoid lysine loss.</p></li><li data-start="3683" data-end="3748"><p data-start="3685" data-end="3748">Use appropriate PPE (mask, goggles) to prevent dust exposure.</p></li></ul><hr data-start="3750" data-end="3753" /><h2 data-start="3755" data-end="3782">5. Packaging &amp; Storage</h2><ul data-start="3783" data-end="4123"><li data-start="3783" data-end="3872"><p data-start="3785" data-end="3872">Packaging: 25 kg carton drums, kraft bags with PE liner, or jumbo bags (500–1000 kg).</p></li><li data-start="3873" data-end="3971"><p data-start="3875" data-end="3971">Storage: keep sealed, dry, at ambient temperature, away from heat, moisture, and direct sunlight.</p></li><li data-start="3972" data-end="4033"><p data-start="3974" data-end="4033">Shelf life: 24 months unopened under recommended storage.</p></li><li data-start="4034" data-end="4123"><p data-start="4036" data-end="4123">Safety: dust may cause irritation; handle with ventilation and protective equipment.</p></li></ul><hr data-start="4125" data-end="4128" /><h2 data-start="4130" data-end="4166">6. Comparison with L-Lysine HCl</h2><ul data-start="4167" data-end="4524"><li data-start="4167" data-end="4293"><p data-start="4169" data-end="4293"><strong data-start="4169" data-end="4189">Purity vs dosage</strong>: L-Lysine HCl contains 98.5% salt (~78% lysine), requires a lower inclusion rate but is more expensive.</p></li><li data-start="4294" data-end="4406"><p data-start="4296" data-end="4406"><strong data-start="4296" data-end="4309">Economics</strong>: L-Lysine Sulphate provides similar nutritional value at a lower cost per unit of usable lysine.</p></li><li data-start="4407" data-end="4524"><p data-start="4409" data-end="4524"><strong data-start="4409" data-end="4425">Practicality</strong>: Both are highly bioavailable; choice depends on feed mill economics and formulation precision.</p></li></ul><hr data-start="4526" data-end="4529" /><h2 data-start="4531" data-end="4572">7. Quality Control (Buyer Checklist)</h2><ul data-start="4573" data-end="4846"><li data-start="4573" data-end="4662"><p data-start="4575" data-end="4662">Test items: lysine content, moisture, ash, particle size, heavy metals, microbiology.</p></li><li data-start="4663" data-end="4759"><p data-start="4665" data-end="4759">Methods: HPLC for amino acid content, ICP-MS for heavy metals, and standard ISO/GB for microbes.</p></li><li data-start="4760" data-end="4846"><p data-start="4762" data-end="4846">Documents: COA, SDS, heavy metal &amp; microbiological reports provided with shipment.</p></li></ul><hr data-start="5192" data-end="5195" /><h2 data-start="5197" data-end="5224">9. Specification Table</h2><div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse" tabindex="-1"><table class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" data-start="5226" data-end="5748"><thead data-start="5226" data-end="5242"><tr data-start="5226" data-end="5242"><th data-start="5226" data-end="5233" data-col